B.Uf=new A.bs("Constraints Rule Flow","FLUTTER CORE","LAYOUT RULES","The Flutter layout engine is governed by a singular unidirectional layout rule:\n\u2022 Constraints go DOWN: Parent forces bounding parameters (minWidth, maxWidth, minHeight, maxHeight) on children.\n\u2022 Sizes go UP: Children compute geometry dimensions within boundaries and pass final sizes up to parents.\n\u2022 Parent sets position: Parent places children on coordinates grid based on layout properties.","BoxConstraints(\n  minWidth: 100,\n  maxWidth: double.infinity,\n  minHeight: 50,\n  maxHeight: 120,\n)",B.Om)
